# Implementation Plan - Number Plate Detection System

## Goal Description
Create a complete, production-ready desktop software for Number Plate Detection using Python. The system will feature a **Modern UI** (using PyQt-Fluent-Widgets), support for **Live Camera** and **Video/Image File** inputs, and a local **SQLite Database**. Optimizations for "Mid CPU" logic will include using `onnxruntime` for inference and `QThread` for non-blocking UI.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Technology Stack Choice**: I have selected **PyQt6** with **PyQt-Fluent-Widgets** to achieve the "Modern and Beautiful" requirement while maintaining native performance on Windows. This avoids the heavy overhead of a browser-based (Electron) app, ensuring smoother performance on a mid-range CPU.

> [!NOTE]
> **Model Usage**: The system will use the existing [models/best.onnx](file:///d:/FYPs/Number%20Plate%20Detection%20System/models/best.onnx). I assume this is a YOLO-based ONNX export. I will use `onnxruntime` for inference.

## Proposed Changes

### Project Structure (New)
I will create the following directory structure:
```text
NPDS/
├── core/
│   ├── detector.py       # wrapper for onnxruntime
│   ├── ocr.py            # wrapper for EasyOCR/PaddleOCR
│   └── video_thread.py   # QThread for video capture
├── database/
│   ├── db_manager.py     # SQLite management
│   └── schema.sql        # Database tables
├── ui/
│   ├── main_window.py    # Main Application Window
│   └── pages/            # Individual pages (Dashboard, Home, Settings)
├── assets/               # Icons, images
└── main.py               # Entry point
```

### Database
#### [NEW] `database/db_manager.py`
- **Tables**:
    - `plates`: id, number_text, confidence, timestamp, image_path, source (camera/video).
    - `logs`: system events (start, stop, errors).
- **Optimization**: Use connection pooling or singleton pattern. Ensure writes are done in a separate thread if high frequency.

### Core Logic
#### [NEW] `core/detector.py`
- Class `PlateDetector`: Loads [best.onnx](file:///d:/FYPs/Number%20Plate%20Detection%20System/models/best.onnx).
- Method `detect(frame)`: Returns bounding boxes and class IDs.
- Optimization: Resize frame to model input size (e.g., 640x640) efficiently.

#### [NEW] `core/ocr.py`
- Class `OCREngine`: Loads OCR model.
- Method `recognize(plate_crop)`: Returns text.
- Validation: Filter results to match Pakistani plate formats (e.g., ABC-1234).

### User Interface
#### [NEW] `ui/main_window.py`
- Using `qfluentwidgets.FluentWindow`.
- Navigation items: Home (Dashboard), Live View, Media Scan, Database.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will run the application and verify it launches without errors.
- `python main.py`

### Manual Verification
- **Live Feed**: Connect a webcam (or dummy video) and verify 30fps+ rendering.
- **Scanning**: Drop a video file and check if plates are detected and saved to DB.
- **Database**: Open the "Records" page and see if entries populate.
